; name: Two-sided cutting board
; group: Kitchen & gifts
; description: A maple cutting board made from both sides: a juice groove round the top with a Ø6 ball nose; then dowel holes on the board’s centre line, in the margin at both ends, before the program stops for you to turn the board over along X onto dowels in them; then recesses for four rubber feet and the board cut out from the back, held by tabs. The back’s work is drawn where it is on the board, seen through it from the top. Set the size, the thickness, the groove and the feet with the variables.
; 
